msgid "The Geofisica package"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*What the geophysics package adds to EMStudio: the formats it reads, the "
"import panel, the Space, the tools and the Inspector section.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Geofisica** 0.1.0 is a mixed package of the official list of the "
"Extended Matrix: its data are the vocabularies of methods, quantities and"
" anomalies and the colour schemes; its code reads stacks, writes them "
"into the graph and draws them. The tasks are in :doc:`/how-to/bring-in"
"/bring-in-a-geophysical-stack` and :doc:`/how-to/sources/trace-an-"
"anomaly-on-a-slice`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Item"
msgstr ""

msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

msgid "Data"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"vocabularies *anomalie*, *metodi*, *grandezze*; colour schemes grey, "
"viridis, hot, jet; licence CC-BY-4.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "Code"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"module ``geofisica``, for EMStudio and Blender; licence GPL-3.0-or-later;"
" it needs the ``em`` API 1.2 or later"
msgstr ""

msgid "Permission"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**files**: reads the chosen geophysical stacks and writes their slice "
"cache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where it writes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the graph, and the cache of pictures in the plugins' own folder (see :doc"
":`file-locations`); never beside the stack"
msgstr ""

msgid "Formats"
msgstr ""

msgid "The format is read from the files, or chosen in **Format**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Format"
msgstr ""

msgid "What the package reads"
msgstr ""

msgid "**CSV grids**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the GPR slices exported as CSV, the step of the grid in the header, the "
"depth in the name"
msgstr ""

msgid "**ASCII matrices**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"matrices of numbers without a header (``.asc``), ``0`` for no value; the "
"size on the ground given in the panel; the vertical sections (``VERT…``) "
"with their length and depth"
msgstr ""

msgid "**XYZV volumes**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"points with a value, divided into planes; a derived resource, not a drawn"
" document"
msgstr ""

msgid "**XYZ lines**"
msgstr ""

msgid "XYZ files in blocks ``line N``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**GeoTIFF rasters**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"float rasters with their georeference, no-value cells, saturated cells "
"reported, a world file checked against the file's own tags"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Pictures**"
msgstr ""

msgid "pictures of slices, the size on the ground given in the panel"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Screen captures**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"pictures captured from the screen of a geophysics program, with the frame"
" from pixels to metres declared once for the whole stack, in the panel: "
"what the plot's ticks stand for, and their pixels or nothing (measured on"
" the first capture)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The depth of a slice is read from its name, in metres, centimetres or "
"millimetres. A product without a depth (an average over the stack, say) "
"lies at the ground."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where it appears"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where"
msgstr ""

msgid "What"
msgstr ""

msgid "``File ▸ Porta dentro una cartella…``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Geophysical stack**: reads a folder and opens the panel with it"
msgstr ""

msgid "``File ▸ Porta dentro…``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``.asc`` and ``.xyz`` go to the package; ``.csv``, ``.tif``, ``.tiff``, "
"``.jpg``, ``.jpeg``, ``.png`` offer **Read as:** **Geofisica · "
"Geophysical stack** beside **EMStudio (as it is)**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The panel **Geophysical stack**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the import (below)"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space**, **Visibility ▾** ▸ **Plugin layers**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the stacks as planes, with the depth cursor over the scene"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space**, the **Outliner**, under **No epoch**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Slice stacks**: a row for each stack drawn"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Space**, the bar over the scene"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Point anomaly on a slice**, **Linear anomaly on a slice**, **Areal "
"anomaly on a slice**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Inspector**"
msgstr "**מפקח**"

msgid "the section **Geophysical reading**, on a slice, a section or an anomaly"
msgstr ""

msgid "The import panel"
msgstr ""

msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Folder**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the stack's folder; ``File ▸ Porta dentro una cartella…`` writes it here"
msgstr ""

msgid "**What it is**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"what the package found: stack, format, slices, sections, depths, method, "
"the frame of the screen captures, what is missing, the documents of this "
"stack already in the graph"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Method**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**as the format suggests**, **GPR (ground-penetrating radar)**, **ERT "
"(electrical resistivity)**, **Magnetometry**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Format**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**read from the files**, or one of the formats above"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Stack name**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"empty: the folder's name. It is the stack's identity: keep it the same to"
" import again"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Quantity**, **Unit**"
msgstr ""

msgid "what the values measure, and in which unit"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Width (x)**, **Height (y)**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the size of a slice on the ground, in metres"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Sections**"
msgstr ""

msgid "length × depth of each line, as ``VERT1=92x8, VERT4=50x8``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Every section: length**, **Every section: depth**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the same size for every section, in metres"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Captures: x ticks**, **Captures: y ticks**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"what the plot's first and last ticks stand for, in metres, as ``-50 25`` "
"and ``-22 37``. Written, they make the format **Screen captures**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Captures: frame in pixels**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"left, top, right, bottom of those ticks on the capture, as ``610, 170, "
"1303, 715``; empty: measured on the first capture"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Origin (E, N)**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"where x = 0, y = 0 lies, as ``701806.741, 4234824.081``; kept to the "
"millimetre"
msgstr ""

msgid "**EPSG**"
msgstr ""

msgid "the code of the origin's reference system, as ``25830``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**The origin, according to**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**not said**, **the instrument (its own coordinates)**, **a documentation"
" (figure, plan, report)**, **by eye**: it gives the axis *geometry* of "
"the slices, *reality based*, *observable* or *asserted*"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Values in the file**, **…stand for**, **…in**, **…according to**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the declared scale: the file's range (``1-255``), what it stands for "
"(``0-3500``), the unit (``ohm.m``), and where the scale comes from"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Colours**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**the method's**, **grey**, **viridis**, **hot**, **jet**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Colour range**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**as the format suggests**, **one for the whole stack**, **one per slice**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Where the slices are, according to**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**the source of the position**, **the instrument (reality based)**, **a "
"documentation (observable)**, **by eye (asserted)**"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Placement (JSON)**"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"advanced: ``{\"origin\": [E, N], \"rotation\": 0, \"epsg\": 32633, "
"\"source\": \"figure\"}``"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Import**"
msgstr ""

msgid "writes the stack into the graph, as one step"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A word written in a field wins over the same key in **Placement (JSON)**."
" A wrong word is refused with its reason, and nothing is written: ticks "
"on one axis only, a frame that is not four pixels, an EPSG that is not a "
"code, an EPSG or a source without an origin (**the EPSG or the source "
"alone place nothing**), captures without a frame, a frame not found on "
"the first capture (**write its pixels**)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The stack in the Space"
msgstr ""

msgid "Control"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

msgid "The depth cursor"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"over the scene: the stack, the slice, its depth below ground, its place "
"(``4/6``); **▲** / **▼**, or :kbd:`↑` / :kbd:`↓` with the focus"
msgstr ""

msgid "The row of the stack"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"in **Visibility ▾**: shown or hidden, opacity, mode, slice, **sections "
"(n)**, where the stack lies"
msgstr ""

msgid "The row in the Outliner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"under **No epoch** ▸ **Slice stacks**, with its slices and sections (``6 "
"slices, 6 sections``): the eye shows or hides the stack in every Space "
"open, a click selects its acquisition"
msgstr ""

msgid "**All**, **One at a time**, **Down to**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"every slice, the cursor's slice, the slices down to the cursor's. Over 60"
" planes they are shown one at a time; **Down to** shows at most 60"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where it lies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"in the world when the stack has an origin and the study a georeference in"
" the same EPSG; otherwise **in its own frame**, with the reason (**not "
"placed in the world**, **the study has no georeference**, **another EPSG "
"than the study's**)"
msgstr ""

msgid "The tracing tools"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tool"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it writes"
msgstr ""

msgid "**◉ Point anomaly on a slice**"
msgstr ""

msgid "a point, at the first click"
msgstr ""

msgid "**〰 Linear anomaly on a slice**"
msgstr ""

msgid "a line; a double click, **✓** or :kbd:`Enter` closes it"
msgstr ""

msgid "**▱ Areal anomaly on a slice**"
msgstr ""

msgid "an area; a double click, **✓** or :kbd:`Enter` closes it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While you trace, the points placed are drawn on the plane in yellow, and "
"the bar counts them (**Linear anomaly on a slice: 1 point**). :kbd:`Esc` "
"or **✕** stops. A tool is put down when the Space shows another document."
" Each trace writes a unit **USD**, its properties (kind of anomaly, "
"method, top and bottom of the band, confidence when given), and an "
"extractor of the slice, or a combiner of the extractors of several "
"slices. The kinds of anomaly are **point anomaly**, **linear anomaly**, "
"**areal anomaly**, **diffraction hyperbola**, **high-resistivity zone**, "
"**low-resistivity zone**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once written, the anomaly stays drawn on each slice it was read on, in "
"cyan: a dot for a point, a line, a closed outline for an area, with its "
"vertices. It follows the plane: on a section along its line, on a slice "
"at its depth."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Inspector section"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Geophysical reading** appears on a document of a stack and on a unit "
"traced on the slices."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Geophysical reading section of the Inspector on a slice of the "
"Basilica Iulia: method ERT, horizontal slice, depth 1.00–1.50 m below "
"ground, electrical resistivity, the declared scale, the values in the "
"file, observable, extent, stack, file, identity and stamp."
msgstr ""

msgid "On"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rows"
msgstr ""

msgid "A slice or a section"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Method**, **What**, **Depth**, **Quantity**, **Scale of the values**, "
"**Values in the file**, **Where it lies**, **Extent**, **Stack**, "
"**File**, **Identity**, **Stamp**"
msgstr ""

msgid "An anomaly"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Anomaly**, **Read on**, **Through**, **Bands**, **Slice**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A stack that cannot be read is answered with its reason, in the language "
"of the interface: **the stack X cannot be read: …**."
msgstr ""

